LEGO Collection Manager (Windows portable)
==========================================

Thank you for using LEGO Collection Manager!

QUICK START
-----------
1. Unzip this folder anywhere (for example Desktop\LEGO-Collection-Manager).
2. Double-click "Launch LEGO Collection Manager.bat".
3. Your web browser opens the app. Keep the black window open while you use it.

YOUR COLLECTION DATA
--------------------
Your database and logs are stored in the "data" folder next to this README.
When you upgrade to a newer ZIP, copy your old "data" folder (and config.env if
you created one) into the new folder. Do not delete "data" unless you want a
fresh empty collection.

REBRICKABLE SYNC (OPTIONAL)
---------------------------
To download set data from Rebrickable:
1. Create a free API key at https://rebrickable.com/api/
2. Copy "config.env.example" to "config.env" in this folder.
3. Open "config.env" in Notepad and paste your key after REBRICKABLE_API_KEY=
4. Save the file and launch the app again.

TROUBLESHOOTING
---------------
- "Windows protected your PC" / SmartScreen: click More info, then Run anyway.
  This app is not code-signed yet.
- Port already in use: close other copies of the app, or edit config.env and set
  LCM_PORT=8001 (then open http://127.0.0.1:8001/ in your browser).
- Blank page: wait a few seconds and refresh. Check that the "data" folder exists.
- Antivirus blocked the app: allow "lcm-server.exe" in your security software.

